      "content": "#include <bits/stdc++.h>\n\nusing namespace std;\nusing ll = long long;\n\nconstexpr size_t HASH_CAPACITY = 2048;\nconstexpr size_t HASH_MASK = HASH_CAPACITY - 1;\n\nstruct PrefixSlot {\n  ll key;\n  int count;\n  int generation;\n};\n\nstatic inline size_t hash_index(ll key) {\n  uint64_t x = static_cast<uint64_t>(key);\n  x ^= x >> 30;\n  x *= 0xbf58476d1ce4e5b9ULL;\n  x ^= x >> 27;\n  x *= 0x94d049bb133111ebULL;\n  x ^= x >> 31;\n  return static_cast<size_t>(x) & HASH_MASK;\n}\n\nstatic inline int prefix_count(const PrefixSlot *table, ll key, int generation) {\n  size_t pos = hash_index(key);\n  while (table[pos].generation == generation) {\n    if (table[pos].key == key)\n      return table[pos].count;\n    pos = (pos + 1) & HASH_MASK;\n  }\n  return 0;\n}\n\nstatic inline void add_prefix(PrefixSlot *table, ll key, int generation) {\n  size_t pos = hash_index(key);\n  while (table[pos].generation == generation && table[pos].key != key)\n    pos = (pos + 1) & HASH_MASK;\n  if (table[pos].generation != generation) {\n    table[pos].generation = generation;\n    table[pos].key = key;\n    table[pos].count = 0;\n  }\n  ++table[pos].count;\n}\n\nll solve(const vector<int> &matrix, int short_dim, int long_dim, int k) {\n  vector<ll> band(long_dim, 0);\n  PrefixSlot table[HASH_CAPACITY] = {};\n  int generation = 0;\n  ll answer = 0;\n\n  for (int first = 0; first < short_dim; ++first) {\n    fill(band.begin(), band.end(), 0);\n    for (int last = first; last < short_dim; ++last) {\n      const int *row = matrix.data() + static_cast<size_t>(last) * long_dim;\n      for (int x = 0; x < long_dim; ++x)\n        band[x] += row[x];\n\n      ++generation;\n      add_prefix(table, 0, generation);\n      ll prefix = 0;\n      for (int x = 0; x < long_dim; ++x) {\n        prefix += band[x];\n        answer += prefix_count(table, prefix - k, generation);\n        add_prefix(table, prefix, generation);\n      }\n    }\n  }\n  return answer;\n}\n\nint main() {\n  ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n  cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n  int k, m, n;\n  if (!(cin >> k >> m >> n))\n    return 0;\n\n  const int short_dim = min(m, n);\n  const int long_dim = max(m, n);\n  vector<int> matrix(static_cast<size_t>(short_dim) * long_dim);\n\n  if (m <= n) {\n    for (int i = 0; i < m; ++i)\n      for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j)\n        cin >> matrix[static_cast<size_t>(i) * long_dim + j];\n  } else {\n    for (int i = 0; i < m; ++i) {\n      for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n        int value;\n        cin >> value;\n        matrix[static_cast<size_t>(j) * long_dim + i] = value;\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  cout << solve(matrix, short_dim, long_dim, k) << '\\n';\n  return 0;\n}\n",
      "path": "src/main.cpp"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Pairing boundaries along the smaller dimension reduces the amount of enumeration on tall or wide matrices. Storing each paired slice contiguously and using a compact generation-tagged prefix table should also improve locality and avoid repeated hash-node allocation.",
  "notes": "The compact table has 2048 slots; for valid dimensions it stores at most long_dim + 1 <= 1000 distinct prefixes per generation. Prefix sums and the result use signed 64-bit values, preserving correctness with negative entries.",
  "sources_kept": [],
  "transformations": [
    "Store the matrix in an orientation where the smaller dimension is the paired-boundary axis and each scanned slice is contiguous.",
    "Replace 2D row-prefix construction and unordered_map counting with rolling band sums and a compact generation-tagged linear-probing prefix table."
  ]
